WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:56.050
<b>Finale</b>

3
00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.350
What? They ran
away and left the island?

4
00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:57.360
Yes.

5
00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.610
We couldn't even give them our gift.

6
00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.070
How disappointing.

7
00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.070
And after all they did for us.

8
00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:07.070
I wonder if they realize how
much we appreciate them.

9
00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:10.930
I agree.

10
00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.810
They don't know how we feel.

11
00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.060
You know, Aisa, it's not fair
that you were the only one

12
00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:20.980
that got to say goodbye to them.

13
00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:24.320
Everyone's really upset that we
let our heroes just run away.

14
00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.700
Sorry! Luffy and the others made
me promise to keep it a secret!

15
00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.130
Did you

16
00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.880
Luffy can stretch his body really far!

17
00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:37.800
He's like a "Gum-Gum Pistol!"
Kapow! Yay!

18
00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.640
Aisa, please! You've got to hold still!

19
00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.190
I never knew there were warriors
like him in the Blue Sea!

20
00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:46.520
I wanna be just
like him when I grow up.

21
00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.900
A Gum-Gum warrior!

22
00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:51.070
Aisa.

23
00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:52.490
Hm?

24
00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:54.360
I'm just going to
trim your hair a little.

25
00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.240
You need to let it grow.

26
00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:56.990
Huh?

27
00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.760
Hey, it'll look good.

28
00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:01.680
I think you've forgotten you're
a girl, and girls should look cute.

29
00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.560
What? Cute? Me?

30
00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.640
Are you nuts?

31
00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.850
I'm not!

32
00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.670
With the war over, there's no need for
kids like you to carry weapons anymore.

33
00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:20.660
Now you can enjoy life the way it was
meant to be and as a proper young lady.

34
00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.070
I never knew you were so ladylike!

35
00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:26.660
Come on, Aisa! Now hold still!

36
00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:27.870
Laki's ladylike!

37
00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:28.790
Aisa!

38
00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.990
Great Warrior Kalgara.

39
00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:43.490
We were told that the Shandorians'
role has been fulfilled.

40
00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:48.900
As for your last wish it was
delivered to your best friend.

41
00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:52.690
Our future generations will
no longer have to shed blood.

42
00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:55.110
We are finally at peace.

43
00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:56.690
The war may be over.

44
00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:59.240
But one thing that will
never end is our pride!

45
00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:03.240
Please continue to guide us, Mighty
Kalgara, and watch over us as well.

46
00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:09.330
We solemnly swear, The Fire
of Shandora will never die!

47
00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:21.750
I-I cannot abandon my duties!

48
00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.500
I am the Sky Knight, after all.

49
00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:25.810
Perhaps you should
be looking at yourself.

50
00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.860
Remember, this city originally
belonged to your people.

51
00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:31.510
It did, long ago.

52
00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:33.730
But that means nothing now.

53
00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:37.140
In fact, with this battle, all
of us realized something.

54
00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:39.020
Vearth belongs to no group.

55
00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.920
It must be shared.

56
00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.300
Our world has two sides.

57
00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.380
The land is called Skypiea.

58
00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.460
The city, Shandora.

59
00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.450
They have been torn
asunder by war for ages.

60
00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:55.790
Only a man who has long lamented that
war can unite them, and that man is you.

61
00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:59.490
So Sky Knight, Gan Fall.

62
00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:02.360
I'd like you to take
Skypiea's throne again.

63
00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:07.600
Only you can heal the deep wounds
that scar this land of ours.

64
00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.230
We'd like you to do it, too, sir!

65
00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:10.520
Gan Fall, please!

66
00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:14.070
We Shandorians are behind
you all the way Yeah!

67
00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.570
Gan Fall!

68
00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:16.570
Our god!

69
00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:17.820
Please come back!

70
00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:22.730
Well, well.

71
00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.870
And here I was thinking
that I'd finally be able

72
00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:29.410
to get some rest and
tend to my pumpkin patch.

73
00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:50.910
<b>Lower Skypiea,
the White Sea</b>

74
00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:57.320
Okay! We're almost there!

75
00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:00.370
Everyone! See that up ahead?

76
00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:01.580
That's Cloud End!

77
00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:02.740
Whoa, lemme see!

78
00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:04.660
Huh.

79
00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:06.450
So that's where we go back down from?

80
00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:09.100
We got here sooner than I thought.

81
00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.980
Aww. We really have to go back already?

82
00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:17.910
You know, it sounds crazy, but I'm
actually gonna miss this place.

83
00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.450
I think it's time we said
goodbye to the White Sea.

84
00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:22.620
Sky island sure is fun.

85
00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:24.540
But scary, too.

86
00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:27.250
We just go through that gate,
and there'll be a Milky Road that'll take us

87
00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.750
to the Blue Sea, huh?

88
00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:32.210
Wonder if we'll ever
visit this place again.

89
00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:34.000
Well, you never know.

90
00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.950
I'm sorry, but this
is as far as we can go!

91
00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:47.200
Goodbye, my friends!

92
00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.840
Take care of yourselves!

93
00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:49.540
Suu!

94
00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:51.040
We will! Thanks for the escort!

95
00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:54.500
Conis! Don't forget me, angel!

96
00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.540
Say goodbye to the others for us!

97
00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:58.900
See ya!

98
00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:00.800
It was nice meeting you guys!

99
00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.720
Thanks for everything!

100
00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:05.100
No! You've got it wrong!

101
00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.270
We're the ones who
should be thanking you!

102
00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:09.810
We'll never forget you!

103
00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:11.230
Thanks to you all!

104
00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:13.320
Goodbye, Conis, old guy, furball!

105
00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:14.190
Take care now!

106
00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:15.190
– Bye!
– Bye!

107
00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:16.980
Now take in your sails,
and hold on tight!

108
00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.740
You're in for a bumpy ride!

109
00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:22.240
Right! Let's do as the man says!

110
00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.240
It feels like we're
already picking up speed!

111
00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:28.090
Yeah, and we're sliding down from
thousands of feet in the air! Hurry up!

112
00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.090
– Aye!
– Aye!

113
00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:30.960
– Huh?
– Huh?

114
00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:35.440
Wh-What the...?

115
00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.420
He says, "Don't leave without me."

116
00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:41.670
Oh.

117
00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.800
That's the Southbird we
brought up here with us.

118
00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:51.300
Captain! It looks like the log pose has
the coordinates for the next island!

119
00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.390
Great! Let's go!

120
00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:58.690
Once we get to the bottom, we're
gonna start a brand-new adventure!

121
00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:00.770
Who's up for finding some gold?

122
00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:02.770
Guys! Get ready!

123
00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:07.620
Blue Sea, here we come!

124
00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:08.910
– Aye!
– Aye!

125
00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:24.010
Everyone grab hold of something!

126
00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:26.140
The freefall's about to start!

127
00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:45.630
Just hang on!

128
00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:49.460
One Octopus Balloon, on the way!

129
00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.090
A balloon!

130
00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:27.000
Yeah! Ain't it great?

131
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.370
We're not falling!

132
00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:29.670
Oh, good!

133
00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.920
For a minute there,
I thought we were goners!

134
00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.000
All of us!

135
00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:02.160
Keep ringing it!

136
00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:07.040
Let the departing heroes of this land
know how much we appreciate them!

137
00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.290
Heso!

138
00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:13.630
Luffy! Come back soon!

139
00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.340
You're always welcome!

140
00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.840
Thank you so much!

141
00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:19.510
We wish you
safe passage to the Blue Sea!

142
00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:29.610
When you look up, you see the sky.

143
00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:33.410
Though some believe
it to be only a legend,

144
00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:37.370
there is an island floating
thousands of feet in the air.

145
00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:41.040
If you listen carefully,
you can hear the tolling of a bell.

146
00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:45.880
It rings today, and it
will ring again tomorrow.

147
00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:51.180
That bell rings from the heavens,
from a land that wandered.

148
00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.760
It sings of its pride, and proclaims

149
00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:58.690
to the rest of the world,
"We are here."

150
00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:01.790
This is so great!

151
00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:03.120
Tell me about it!

152
00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:05.790
What a way to travel! I love it!

153
00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:10.980
You're calling off the search?

154
00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:12.790
Of course.

155
00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:14.830
The City of Gold has been
in the sky this whole time.

156
00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:17.540
There's nothing else to be
found at the bottom of the sea.

157
00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:21.020
Sorry, fellas. This dream's over.

158
00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:23.270
No point in staying here anymore.

159
00:11:23.270 --> 00:11:24.750
Old man.

160
00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.630
Cricket.

161
00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:31.140
I wanna thank all of you for helping me
pursue my dream for all of these years.

162
00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:33.230
You never stopped believing.

163
00:11:33.230 --> 00:11:34.210
That means a lot.

164
00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:35.540
Does this mean...

165
00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:38.170
...you're leaving the Alliance?

166
00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:39.300
Hey, guys.

167
00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:44.720
Since this dream's done, which
one are we gonna pursue next?

168
00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:54.360
We'll all follow you to
the ends of the earth, Old Man!

169
00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:55.490
Yeah!

170
00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:03.060
– Gold! Gold! Gold! Gold!
– Gold! Gold! Gold! Gold!

171
00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:05.770
We finally struck it rich!

172
00:12:05.770 --> 00:12:08.100
What should we buy with all this loot?

173
00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:11.310
Hey! I know! A huge bronze statue!

174
00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.610
Moron!

175
00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:14.650
Only an idiot would
exchange gold for bronze!

176
00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:15.780
How stupid!

177
00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:17.530
What we need are more cannons!

178
00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:19.030
Ten of them! Ten!

179
00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:21.510
Nami, I want to buy
a refrigerator with a lock!

180
00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:22.210
Uh-uh!

181
00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:23.500
If you get one with a lock,
there'll be no way

182
00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:25.980
for me to get a midnight snack!

183
00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:28.360
That's exactly why I want one, you pig!

184
00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:30.780
Would you guys just hold on a second?

185
00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:32.320
We need to land first.

186
00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:34.410
Then we can divide up the treasure.

187
00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.790
Please buy me books!

188
00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:40.960
If we buy everything you guys want,
we're gonna be broke again in no time.

189
00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:52.000
The sun's completely set now.

190
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.590
It's still a nice view.

191
00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:56.750
You're right. It really is.

192
00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:12.250
Agh! That's cold!

193
00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:14.540
Nami! Robin! Are you okay?

194
00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.000
That was really scary!

195
00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.630
What happened to the octopus?

196
00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:22.380
Guess it ran out of air.

197
00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:24.130
Wonder how that happened.

198
00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:29.050
Hey, come on!

199
00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:31.640
Don't whine.
We did make it down here alive!

200
00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:32.640
You're right.

201
00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:39.750
And we got to see an incredible place.

202
00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:44.430
Now that we're down
here, it looks so far away.

203
00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:46.840
Like something out of a dream.

204
00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:48.640
It's a dreamland.

205
00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.340
Think we'll see it again?

206
00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:53.080
Well, you might see some
place similar when you die.

207
00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:53.960
Not you.

208
00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:56.040
I doubt you're going any place good!

209
00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.380
You jerk!

210
00:13:57.380 --> 00:13:59.860
You guys keep discussing the afterlife.

211
00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:02.120
Me? I'm gonna go
put on a pot of coffee.

212
00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:03.830
Make dinner instead, Sanji!

213
00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:05.120
Are you ever not hungry?

214
00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:07.550
Have some coffee first
and be patient, will ya!

215
00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:09.630
pirate treasure is always divided up.

216
00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:11.340
Even after splitting up the loot,

217
00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:13.470
we'd all have more gold than
we'd know what to do with.

218
00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:18.060
Ones that that'll teach me all about

219
00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:21.150
the latest medical
procedures and operations!

220
00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:23.380
I wanna buy a bunch
of new medical books!

221
00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:26.720
New pots, frying pans,
silverware, giant mousetrap...

222
00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:30.370
Wow, even after all that,
there'll still be a lot left over.

223
00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:32.420
– Right.
– Uh-huh.

224
00:14:30.860 --> 00:14:32.420
I could buy lotsa booze.

225
00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:35.670
But first, I take an
extra cut: 80 percent!

226
00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:37.170
– Are you nuts?!
– Are you nuts?!

227
00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:38.840
It's not for me.

228
00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:41.430
Oh, yeah? Then who? And why
should they receive a bigger

229
00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:43.010
share than the rest of us, huh?!

230
00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:46.170
It's for a special lady.
We're going to set aside

231
00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:48.960
the gold to pay for the
repairs we need to make.

232
00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:52.100
A lady? Oh, wait, you mean the Merry?

233
00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:53.690
That's right.

234
00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:56.100
Isn't it about time we paid her
back for all she's done for us?

235
00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:57.690
Well, come to think of it,

236
00:14:57.690 --> 00:15:00.900
the Going Merry has carried us
for a long time now, hasn't she?

237
00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:04.060
Ever since I joined up and left
my village in the East Blue.

238
00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:07.440
And that's exactly why we need
to give her some tender, loving care.

239
00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:11.150
Good idea!
The Going Merry's Great Repair!

240
00:15:11.150 --> 00:15:12.660
Let's do it!

241
00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.230
Here. Dig in.

242
00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:19.900
Huh. I've been wondering how much longer
Usopp's half-ass repairs were gonna last.

243
00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:21.920
Hey, I'm a sniper, not a shipwright!

244
00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:25.040
Yeah, right. It's time we took
the Merry to a real shipyard,

245
00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:29.260
and got some honest-to- goodness shipwrights
to give her the repairs she needs.

246
00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.410
So, there are people who can
fix ships better than Usopp?

247
00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:36.680
Yep! Sometimes when you need a job done
right, you've gotta go see a professional!

248
00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.100
That's it!

249
00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.710
We've gotta get a
shipwright for our crew!

250
00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:43.560
Our journey's far from over, right?

251
00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:45.310
– Mm.
– Mm.

252
00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:47.760
We really need
someone with those skills.

253
00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:50.120
And the Merry isn't just our ship!

254
00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:51.740
She's our home, too!

255
00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:55.270
So let's go find us a shipwright
who can keep the Merry safe!

256
00:15:57.800 --> 00:15:59.350
Well, I'm impressed.

257
00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:01.460
Whoa. He got to the point.

258
00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:03.040
That's pretty rare.

259
00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:06.220
Well, that sounds really good
to me, Luffy! Let's go do it!

260
00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:07.980
Uh... That's what I just said!

261
00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.530
I just hope we can find somebody good!

262
00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:12.030
We should get a musician, too!

263
00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:13.960
Let's forget that one.

264
00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:22.340
What's all the ruckus out here?!

265
00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.160
Make way!

266
00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:27.200
Quit pushing! C'mon! Stop it! Lemme go!

267
00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:28.870
Why are they fighting?!

268
00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:42.310
Bellamy!

269
00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:43.690
Sarquiss!

270
00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:45.700
Isn't someone gonna stop them?!

271
00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:49.840
No more! I'm begging you!

272
00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:51.750
Why are you making me do this?!

273
00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:53.150
What the hell is going on?

274
00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.980
I've never seen
Sarquiss plead like that.

275
00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:57.750
Why you ask?

276
00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:02.290
Why am I making you? Sarquiss. Bellamy.

277
00:17:03.890 --> 00:17:10.340
I'm making you do this because you've made
a mockery of this symbol. Heh heh heh...

278
00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:13.720
Does the Sky Island exist or not?

279
00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:17.560
Is the legendary
City of Gold real or not?

280
00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:22.760
The truth doesn't
really matter, now does it.

281
00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:27.320
You play the opposing sides off each
other, to twist them to your will.

282
00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:31.020
That's what I told you. Right, Bellamy?

283
00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:35.450
I think that's, Don Quixote Doflamingo!

284
00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:38.080
He's one of
the Seven Warlords of the Sea!

285
00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:40.710
I heard his bounty's over 300 million.

286
00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.750
What's a guy like him doing here?

287
00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:48.160
You've really let me down and I've got
zero tolerance for useless punks like you.

288
00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:51.890
No! Not again! My body's moving,

289
00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:57.200
on its own, I can't
control it! Please, nooooo!

290
00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.020
– Bellamy!
– Bellamy!

291
00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.160
Please.

292
00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:09.390
Huh?

293
00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:12.770
Just give me one more
chance, to set things right.

294
00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:16.810
I swear we will loyally
follow your every command.

295
00:18:16.810 --> 00:18:17.910
Bellamy!

296
00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:19.810
Let it go, Bellamy!

297
00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:25.630
I might've lost but I have never
once acted against your principles.

298
00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:27.960
I swear on your symbol! Please!

299
00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:30.030
I had reasons for my actions!

300
00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:32.240
I couldn't just let the
Straw Hats get away.

301
00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:36.080
They were bound to find you
someday if I didn't stop them!

302
00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:38.750
Ahhh... What a touching sentiment.

303
00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:40.720
Such genuine loyalty.

304
00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:45.260
Your concern for my well-being
is duly noted, Bellamy.

305
00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:49.450
Heh heh heh... There's a
New Era quickly approaching,

306
00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:52.690
so your actions here
won't really matter.

307
00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:57.100
But, I still have no use for you.

308
00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:02.330
Doflamingooo!

309
00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:13.370
He wiped out Bellamy as easily as stomping
on a baby! He was worth 55 million!

310
00:19:13.370 --> 00:19:14.070
Hehehehe...

311
00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:16.120
The beginning is upon us!

312
00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:20.420
I suggest you prepare. We're
drawing close to a new world

313
00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:23.320
in which only true pirates can survive.

314
00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:27.900
The weak should run while they still can,
or be swept away by the tides of time

315
00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:30.980
as they roll back to reveal
a New Era of Champions!

316
00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:43.280
When you're lost and alone, call out and lead me to your side

317
00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:48.700
As you wander far from home, you search the sky and never hide

318
00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:51.500
You are so much like the moon

319
00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:56.150
Calmer than a star, your twinkling's lost

320
00:19:59.600 --> 00:20:08.550
A deep reflection shines, you slowly leave, fading, and what's the cost?

321
00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:13.780
Stay as you are, don't lose your way

322
00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:22.090
Let my words guide you, and look ahead until the day!

323
00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:28.980
Don't give up on your dreams, through endless nights they come to you

324
00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:34.600
If you stop, you'll never see them shining through!

325
00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:40.370
Will you return? Maybe not... Will you learn? I hope you do

326
00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:46.760
Please put your past to rest, and live your life anew.
